The relevant rule is: *If a container is in front of another container, then objects inside the first container are in front of the second container.*  
Box EEE is behind DDD, so DDD is in front of EEE. All orange and green rectangles are inside or covered by DDD, therefore they are in front of EEE. The white object is inside EEE. An object cannot be in front of itself, so the white object is not in front of the white object. Hence not all objects are in front of the white object.

